<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.11.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00248</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.11.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>01c2c7f5-4625-4cf0-9296-edc141956bcf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">For numbers 1 – 2, use the graph below:</para>
      
        <media alt="This figure a shows a straight line graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The x and y axes run from negative 10 to 10. The line goes through the points (negative 6, negative 8), (negative 4, negative 6), (negative 2, negative 4), (0, negative 2), (2, 0), (4, 2), (6, 4), (8, 6).">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_10_01.jpg"/>
        </media>
      
      <exercise id="_183419ea-c11a-4339-aadb-d9f6fddd56ed" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Correct! The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00006">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0ff195d9-131c-40b6-9d54-694f267a6025" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Correct! The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00011">For numbers 3 – 4, use the graph below:</para>
      
        <media alt="This figure a shows a straight line graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The x and y axes run from negative 10 to 10. The line goes through the points (negative 6, 6), (negative 3, 4), (0, 2), (3, 0), (6, negative 2), and (9, negative 4).">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_10_02.jpg"/>
        </media>
      
      <exercise id="_328040c7-4577-4c54-ba53-f3023e8a8ae7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00013">Correct! The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at (3,0).</para>
          <para id="para-00014">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00015">The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d9f6c4de-fe6a-4f3e-8663-849afb187a67" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00016">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00017">Correct! The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3adaa38d-78ca-4063-bee4-3133a26edf43" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00020">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00021">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> becomes <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_99318492-7d7c-491b-b4ea-a460dfe1073b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00024">What are the coordinates of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00025">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> becomes <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="b15f1dc1-aa05-4cbf-b354-2c2c6129903f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00028">What is the slope of the line <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00029">Correct! The slope is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, calculated from the equation in standard form.</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Try again. Remember the formula for slope in standard form. Use the Equation Editor to express your answer.</para>
          <para id="para-00031">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>. The slope is found by rearranging the equation into slope-intercept form and identifying the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8179854f-8533-4972-b9f9-094d93ae10f2" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00032">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00033">Correct! Compare your answer: In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00035">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fcec07ea-a807-4295-af28-e0b61a16035d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00036">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00037">Correct! Compare your answer: Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00039">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.Solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. In this equation, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5c1e1577-2cff-4350-8771-d6abb4e818c3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00040">Which graph represents the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Explain how you know.</para>
          <para id="para-00041">
            
              <title>a.</title>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_10_03.png"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00042">
            
              <title>b.</title>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_10_04.png"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00043">
            
              <title>c.</title>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_13_10_05.png"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00044">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00045">a</para>
          <para id="para-00046">b</para>
          <para id="para-00047">c</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00048">Correct! Graph a, because the intercepts are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00049">Try again. Revisit activity 1.11.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00050">The correct answer is Graph <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, because the intercepts are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00051">When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is at (0, 3). When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is (4, 0). Graph <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> has these intercepts.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
